# Thousand Moons Crackshot {1}{W} 2/2: "Whenever this creature attacks, you may pay {2}{W}. When you do, tap target creature." On turn 3 it attacks.
# Mox Pearl and Mox Ruby alone (two mana, one of them white) are not enough; with Mox Jet the {2}{W} is paid exactly and the pool is empty. The target is
# chosen once it is paid (CR 603.12): Bot1's own Crackshot and Bot2's Ornithopter are both legal, a noncreature artifact (Mox Jet) is refused, and the
# Ornithopter is chosen: it is tapped, so it cannot block and the Crackshot connects (Bot2 at 18).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Thousand Moons Crackshot
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thousand Moons Crackshot.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Thousand Moons Crackshot > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.PayCost
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.PayCost
? Bot1.Mana = 
! Bot1.Target(Mox Jet)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
